Embedded React: look up the calling worker's render context once per call.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, in the patch order listed there.
Changed files: engine/core/native_renderer.c and engine/rendering/transform.c.
Not proposed upstream: PS5 React maintains this change here.

With render workers installed, every lookup of a worker's buffers or blit
context is a call through the host's worker_id hook, which the compiler cannot
hoist. xform_emit_2d and xform_emit_3d made it once per output pixel, and each
er_blit_* call made it six to ten times. Both now fetch it once per function.
In a sampled 4K desktop tour with eight workers the lookups fell from 2.6% to
0.5% of busy samples. Output is unchanged.

